1
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,950
一场由内而外、由低到高的脑区之旅
An inside-out journey from lowest to highest

2
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:09,150
约 860 亿个神经元，重约 1.4 公斤
~86 billion neurons in about 1.4 kg of tissue

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:12,350
只占体重约 2%，却消耗约 20% 的能量
Just ~2% of body weight, yet ~20% of the body's energy

4
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:15,950
生命的底层系统：呼吸、心跳、觉醒
The life-support layer: breathing, heartbeat, arousal

5
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:19,150
运动协调与精细校准，也参与认知
Coordinates and fine-tunes movement — and cognition

6
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:22,350
感觉信息的中继站，向皮层分发信号
The relay hub that routes signals up to the cortex

7
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:25,550
稳态总调度：体温、饥渴、节律与内分泌
Homeostasis: temperature, hunger, rhythms, hormones

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,750
动作选择与习惯形成，多巴胺奖赏学习
Action selection, habits, dopamine reward learning

9
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:31,950
威胁检测与恐惧，给记忆打上情绪标签
Threat detection and fear; tags memories with emotion

10
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,150
把经历巩固为长期记忆，也负责空间导航
Consolidates memories and supports spatial navigation

11
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:38,350
整合情绪、注意与疼痛，监测冲突与错误
Blends emotion, attention, pain; monitors conflict

12
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:41,550
内脏感受与情绪觉察：感知身体的状态
Interoception and emotional awareness of the body

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,750
视觉加工的起点：边缘、朝向、颜色、运动
Where vision begins: edges, orientation, colour, motion

14
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,950
躯体感觉与空间整合，引导注意与动作
Body sense and spatial integration guide attention

15
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:51,150
听觉、语言理解、物体识别与记忆
Hearing, language, object recognition, memory

16
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:54,350
运动控制、语言表达，以及计划与决策
Movement, speech, planning and decision-making

17
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:57,550
越往上，功能越抽象、越灵活……
The higher up, the more abstract and flexible…

18
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,750
在这条阶梯的顶端，是额叶的最前部
At the top: the very front of the frontal lobe

19
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,950
前额叶皮层（PFC）：最晚成熟，约至 25 岁
The prefrontal cortex (PFC): last to mature, mid-20s

20
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,750
它由多个分工不同的亚区组成
Built from sub-regions, each with its own job

21
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,950
让我们逐一拆解
Let's take them apart, one by one

22
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:13,550
整合目标、规则、情绪与记忆，形成决策
Binds goals, rules, emotion and memory into decisions

23
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:16,750
七个亚区：外侧、前端、腹侧、内侧
Seven sub-regions: lateral, polar, ventral, medial

24
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:19,950
额叶外侧面中部，与顶叶紧密联结
Mid-lateral frontal cortex, linked to parietal cortex

25
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,150
把目标“挂”在脑中：工作记忆与认知控制
Keeps goals online: working memory & cognitive control

26
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:26,350
下额回：左侧含布洛卡区（44/45 区）
Inferior frontal gyrus; Broca's area on the left

27
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:29,550
右侧是“刹车”：反应抑制；左侧：语言生成
Right: the brake (response inhibition). Left: speech

28
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,750
前额叶最前端，在人类中相对更发达
The tip of the PFC, relatively expanded in humans

29
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:35,950
统筹多个子目标，参与多任务与元认知
Coordinates sub-goals; multitasking and metacognition

30
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:39,150
眼眶上方的额叶底面，接收味觉与嗅觉信息
Underside of the frontal lobe, fed by taste and smell

31
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:42,350
给选项“估价”：权衡奖赏与代价，随规则更新
Prices options: weighs reward vs. cost, updates with rules

32
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:45,550
额叶内侧面下部，紧密连接杏仁核与下丘脑
Lower medial surface, wired to amygdala and hypothalamus

33
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:48,750
整合价值与情绪；损伤会使日常决策失常
Integrates value and emotion; lesions derail decisions

34
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:51,950
额叶内侧面上部，邻近辅助运动区
Upper medial surface, beside the supplementary motor area

35
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,150
社会认知枢纽：推测他人意图，区分自我与他人
Social-cognition hub: reads others' intentions

36
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:58,350
环绕胼胝体前部，常被归入广义内侧前额叶
Wraps the corpus callosum; often counted as medial PFC

37
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:01,550
冲突与错误的“警报器”：监测表现、权衡投入
The conflict & error alarm: monitors and weighs effort

38
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,750
前额叶从不单独工作：与深部结构成环路
The PFC never works alone: it loops with deep structures

39
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:07,950
自上而下地调节注意、情绪与行为
Top-down control of attention, emotion and behaviour

40
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:14,350
三大核心执行功能：抑制、更新、转换
Three core executive functions: inhibition, updating, shifting
